  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0128 database contains three tables: businesses, inspections, and violations. The businesses table stores information about businesses, including their name, address, city, postal code, latitude, longitude, phone number, tax code, business certificate, application date, owner name, owner address, owner city, owner state, and owner zip. The inspections table stores information about inspections, including the business ID, score, date, type, and a foreign key reference to the businesses table. The violations table stores information about violations, including the business ID, date, violation type ID, risk category, description, and a foreign key reference to the businesses table. The primary keys for each table are business_id in the businesses table, business_id in the inspections table, and business_id in the violations table. The business_id column in the inspections and violations tables is a foreign key that references the business_id column in the businesses table. The update and delete rules for the foreign keys are CASCADE and RESTRICT, respectively. There are no other indexes or constraints in the schema.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context:\n\nThe project involves the development of a predictive analytics system for the San Francisco Department of Public Health. The system will manage data about food-related businesses, inspections, and violations. This involves predicting unscheduled inspection scores to ensure public health standards are maintained across eateries.\n\nObjectives:\n\n1. Predict inspection scores for unscheduled inspections from 2013 to 2016, with scores ranging from 1 to 100.\n2. Use historical data to enhance the Department's ability to forecast potential public health risks.\n\nStakeholders & Users:\n\n- San Francisco Department of Public Health officials\n- Data analysts and public health inspectors\n- Business owners affected by inspections\n\nFunctional Descriptions:\n\n1. Business Management:\n   - Store and manage data on businesses, including identification, location, and ownership details.\n   \n2. Inspection Record Keeping:\n   - Maintain a log of inspections, including scores, dates, and types.\n   - Facilitate the prediction of future inspection scores based on historical inspection data.\n\n3. Violation Tracking:\n   - Document violations, including type and risk category.\n   - Link violations to businesses and specific inspection events.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions:\n\n- The system should ensure the confidentiality and integrity of business data.\n- Data processing should be efficient to allow timely predictions and analysis.\n- The solution must scale to handle a large volume of data spanning several years of records.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0128.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0128\nCREATE TABLE `businesses` (\n  `business_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `postal_code` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `latitude` decimal(10,6) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `longitude` decimal(10,6) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `tax_code` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `business_certificate` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `application_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `owner_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `owner_address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `owner_city` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `owner_state` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `owner_zip` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`business_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `inspections` (\n  `business_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `score` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`business_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `inspections_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`business_id`) REFERENCES `businesses` (`business_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `violations` (\n  `business_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `violation_type_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `risk_category` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`business_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `violations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`business_id`) REFERENCES `businesses` (`business_id`) ON DELETE RESTRICT ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
